    {
      "id": 46,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "When a reply goes missing",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 12,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### A reply went missing \u2014 recovery recipe\n\nThe counter tells you one send failed. It does **not** tell you which conversation, and the\nreply is not where you would look for it. Verified 2026-09-01 (incident: transcript seq 2241).\n\n**1 \u2014 Find the turn.** The companion plugin writes one `delivery_failed` forensic record per\nfailed send (timestamp, channel, error category; session ids hashed):\n\n```\nssh -p 2222 730op.synology.me\ndocker exec -u node openclaw-openclaw-gateway-1 \\\n  find /home/node/.openclaw -name 'openclaw-task-observability-forensics.jsonl'\n```\n\n**2 \u2014 Recover the text.** The reply survives in the per-agent transcript, a *different* store\nfrom the delivery queue:\n\n```\ndocker exec -u node openclaw-openclaw-gateway-1 sqlite3 \\\n  /home/node/.openclaw/agents/main/agent/openclaw-agent.sqlite \\\n  \"select created_at, substr(event_json,1,600) from transcript_events\n   where created_at > '<T-2min>' and created_at < '<T+2min>'\n   order by seq desc limit 20;\"\n```\n\n**3 \u2014 Do not bother with the delivery queue.** A permanently-failed `delivery_queue_entries`\nrow is a tombstone: `status=failed`, `recovery_state=completed_permanent`, and `session_key`,\n`channel`, `target`, `last_error` and the payload all **NULL**. Nothing links the failed queue\nid back to the transcript row \u2014 step 2's timestamp window is the only join you have.\n\n**Why there is no alert on this.** Alerting rebuild is parked (platform#13). This panel and\nthe stat above are the entire notification path, which is exactly how a red panel sat unread\nthrough the 2026-09-01 drop.\n"
      }
    },
